rsx live draw: 1D textures (TEXTURE_FORMAT dimension 1) decode as width x 1 images with V clamped, instead of binding white.

texture_size and decode_guest_texture accepted dimension 2 (and 3, patch 2011) only, so every 1D unit was bound to the
white fallback. Into the Nexus' full-screen post pass (lobby, draw 15 of frame 3600, nx-7044dd inputs) samples two 512x1
A8R8G8B8 tables in main memory (1:0xC1C600, 1:0xC1A600, format 0xA5) and wrote pure white over the scene (verified by
nx-mwin2: the fogged lobby instead of white). RPCS3 creates a 1D texture for dimension 1 [src:rpcs3-rsx-graph]. The
fragment program samples every 2D-path unit with .xy, so v is whatever the program left there: a height-1 texture
returns row 0 for any finite v under wrap, mirror, clamp and mirror-once, but BORDER blends in the border colour. The
RSX has no t coordinate for a 1D texture, so a 1D unit's V address mode is clamp to edge (decode_sampler and
sampler_key). rsx_tex_1d.h holds both rules; host test port/rc/tests/run_tex_1d_test.sh compares a software 1D fetch
against the Wx1 2D fetch for every u/v, both filters and all wrap codes (and shows the raw BORDER V differs).
ASSUMPTION: a 1D texture with mips picks its level from u's derivative only; the Wx1 texture also sees v's (none of the
seen 1D units has mips). R&C port patch 7045.

